Z||000000||FAXKID||10-16-2000||09:20 PM||||Is there any product that will take scratches out of glass,the kind that <BR>a bad wiper might make?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-16-2000||09:32 PM||||There are some glass shops around that can polish out some of the scratches.  I don't know of any commercial stuff that is available.  Sounds like a job for a pro.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-16-2000||09:50 PM||||People have gotten some pretty bad scratches out of side/back glass. Windshield glass tho is a whole differant animal. That laminated glass is increadibly strong in some ways and just as incredibly weak in others. The odds are real good that if you aren't extremely careful buffing it that it will crack.<P><BR>It depends allot on just how bad they are. (Mine is bad enough I'm just going to get another windshield for it.)<P>Once upon a time I remember jcwhitless(ney) (jcwhitney.com)having a buffing kit for front glass. <A HREF="http://www.eastwoodco.com" TARGET=_blank>Eastwood</A> might have something to. I haven't looked at either in a while.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||10-16-2000||10:22 PM||||An old trick that I have used in the past for light scratches is tooth paste, not he gel stuff but the paste.  It will not be perfect or last forever but oh well it makes it look better <p>[This message has been edited by Hank is Here (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
